  "_README": {
    "purpose": "Hand-built index of procedures in the ISS/Shuttle Medical Checklist (JSC-48031 Generic Rev H, 2001). scripts/split_checklist.py cuts one PDF per entry. Page ranges use the checklist's PRINTED page labels (e.g. 1-36); the splitter maps them to PDF pages.",
    "source_pdf": "Medical Checklist Rev H.pdf",
    "fields": {
      "id": "stable id used by the triage rules and API",
      "title": "procedure name as printed",
      "start / end": "printed page labels, inclusive. Pages are shared where one procedure ends and the next begins.",
      "heading": "text that marks where this procedure starts on its first page (marked 'start here' in the split PDF)",
      "order": "ordering within a tier; lower = earlier. Life threats follow airway > breathing > circulation > disability",
      "related": "procedures this one sends the crew to (e.g. CPR -> oral airway)",
      "reference": "true = supporting procedure (injection technique, side effects); never offered as a first response"
    },
    "REVIEW": "Draft by Claude, 2026-11-15. Page ranges were checked against the PDF by the splitter (it fails if a heading is not found on the start page). Clinical relevance of each mapping needs team review."
  },
